[2026-03-14T21:04:33.188Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J475dXy3FYzgacaWm7kpXb","type":"tool_result","content":"  1027→#### Test: Step 6 — Pricing fields displayed\n  1028→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 5 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1029→- **Expected:** Step 6 is displayed with numeric input fields for: price per night and cleaning fee. The price per night field is required. The cleaning fee defaults to 0. Currency formatting or prefix ($) is shown. The step indicator shows Step 6 of 7.\n  1030→\n  1031→#### Test: Step 6 — Entering pricing information\n  1032→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 6.\n  1033→- **Action:** User enters 150 for price per night and 50 for cleaning fee.\n  1034→- **Expected:** The fields display $150 and $50 respectively.\n  1035→\n  1036→#### Test: Step 6 — Validation requires price per night\n  1037→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 6 with price per night empty or 0.\n  1038→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n  1039→- **Expected:** A validation error appears (e.g., \"Price per night is required and must be greater than 0\"). The form does not advance.\n  1040→\n  1041→#### Test: Step 7 — Review and publish page displayed\n  1042→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 6 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1043→- **Expected:** Step 7 displays a summary of all entered information: property type, title, full address (address, city, state, country), details (guests, bedrooms, beds, bathrooms), selected amenities, photo thumbnails, price per night, and cleaning fee. A \"Publish\" button and \"Back\" button are visible. The step indicator shows Step 7 of 7.\n  1044→\n  1045→#### Test: Step 7 — Review page shows all entered data correctly\n  1046→- **Initial state:** User has filled out all steps: type \"Cabin\", title \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\", address \"123 Pine Rd, Aspen, CO, USA\", 4 guests, 2 bedrooms, 2 beds, 1 bathroom, amenities \"WiFi\" and \"Kitchen\", 2 photos, price $200/night, cleaning fee $75.\n  1047→- **Expected:** The review page displays all of these values accurately. No data is missing or incorrect.\n  1048→\n  1049→#### Test: Publishing a new listing creates the property\n  1050→- **Initial state:** User is on Step 7 (Review) with all data entered correctly.\n  1051→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Publish\" button.\n  1052→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/properties` with the property data, then `POST /api/property-images` for each photo. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Listing published successfully!\"). The form closes. The new property appears in the Listings tab grid. The \"Total Listings\" stat increments by 1.\n  1053→\n  1054→#### Test: Back button navigates to the previous step\n  1055→- **Initial state:** User is on Step 3 of the Add Listing form.\n  1056→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Back\" button.\n  1057→- **Expected:** The form navigates to Step 2. All previously entered data in Step 2 is preserved (city, address, etc. are still filled).\n  1058→\n  1059→#### Test: Cancel button closes the form without saving\n  1060→- **Initial state:** User is on Step 4 of the Add Listing form with data entered in Steps 1–3.\n  1061→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button.\n  1062→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking \"Discard your listing? All entered information will be lost.\" with \"Discard\" and \"Keep Editing\" buttons.\n  1063→\n  1064→#### Test: Confirming cancel discards the listing form\n  1065→- **Initial state:** The discard confirmation dialog is open.\n  1066→- **Action:** User clicks \"Discard\".\n  1067→- **Expected:** The form closes. No API calls are made. The user returns to the Listings tab. No new property is created.\n  1068→\n  1069→#### Test: Dismissing cancel keeps the form open\n  1070→- **Initial state:** The discard confirmation dialog is open.\n  1071→- **Action:** User clicks \"Keep Editing\".\n  1072→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The form remains on the current step with all data preserved.\n  1073→\n  1074→#### Test: Step indicator shows correct progress throughout the form\n  1075→- **Initial state:** User opens the Add Listing form.\n  1076→- **Action:** User navigates through all 7 steps using Next/Back buttons.\n  1077→- **Expected:** The step indicator accurately shows the current step (e.g., \"Step 1 of 7\", \"Step 2 of 7\", etc.) at each stage. Completed steps may show a checkmark or different styling.\n  1078→\n  1079→#### Test: Data persistence across steps when navigating back and forth\n  1080→- **Initial state:** User has filled out Steps 1–5 and is on Step 5.\n  1081→- **Action:** User clicks \"Back\" twice to Step 3, then \"Next\" twice to Step 5.\n  1082→- **Expected:** All data entered in Steps 3, 4, and 5 is preserved after navigating back and forth. No data is lost.\n  1083→\n  1084→#### Test: Add Listing form works correctly on repeated use\n  1085→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. User has already published one listing successfully.\n  1086→- **Action:** User clicks \"Add Listing\" again, fills out all steps, and publishes.\n  1087→- **Expected:** A second property is created successfully. Both properties appear in the Listings tab. The \"Total Listings\" stat shows the correct total.\n  1088→\n  1089→## Page: User Profile (`/profile`)\n  1090→\n  1091→<!-- Components: ProfileForm, BecomeHostButton, UserReviewsList -->\n  1092→\n  1093→### Component: ProfileForm\n  1094→\n  1095→#### Test: Profile page requires login\n  1096→- **Initial state:** User is not logged in.\n  1097→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1098→- **Expected:** The user is redirected to `/login`. The profile page is not displayed.\n  1099→\n  1100→#### Test: Profile page displays current user info\n  1101→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\", bio \"Love traveling!\", phone \"555-1234\", avatar URL \"https://example.com/avatar.jpg\".\n  1102→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1103→- **Expected:** The profile form displays the current values: name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\" (read-only), bio \"Love traveling!\", phone \"555-1234\", and avatar URL \"https://example.com/avatar.jpg\". The avatar image is displayed using the URL.\n  1104→\n  1105→#### Test: Edit name field inline\n  1106→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with name \"Alice Smith\".\n  1107→- **Action:** User clicks the name field, clears it, types \"Alice Johnson\", and clicks the \"Save\" button.\n  1108→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated name. The name field displays \"Alice Johnson\". A success message (e.g., \"Profile updated\") is shown. The Redux user state is updated with the new name.\n  1109→\n  1110→#### Test: Edit bio field inline\n  1111→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with bio \"Love traveling!\".\n  1112→- **Action:** User clicks the bio textarea, clears it, types \"Digital nomad and foodie\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1113→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated bio. The bio field displays \"Digital nomad and foodie\". A success message is shown.\n  1114→\n  1115→#### Test: Edit phone field inline\n  1116→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with phone \"555-1234\".\n  1117→- **Action:** User clicks the phone field, clears it, types \"555-9876\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1118→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated phone. The phone field displays \"555-9876\". A success message is shown.\n  1119→\n  1120→#### Test: Edit avatar URL field inline\n  1121→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with avatar URL \"https://example.com/old-avatar.jpg\".\n  1122→- **Action:** User clicks the avatar URL field, clears it, types \"https://example.com/new-avatar.jpg\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1123→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated avatar URL. The avatar image preview updates to show the new image from \"https://example.com/new-avatar.jpg\". A success message is shown.\n  1124→\n  1125→#### Test: Save with empty name shows validation error\n  1126→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile`.\n  1127→- **Action:** User clears the name field (leaving it empty) and clicks \"Save\".\n  1128→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Name is required\"). No API call is made. The name field is highlighted as invalid.\n  1129→\n  1130→#### Test: Save with invalid avatar URL shows validation error\n  1131→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile`.\n  1132→- **Action:** User enters \"not-a-url\" in the avatar URL field and clicks \"Save\".\n  1133→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid URL\"). No API call is made.\n  1134→\n  1135→#### Test: Profile form fields are functional on repeated edits\n  1136→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with name \"Alice Smith\".\n  1137→- **Action:** User changes the name to \"Alice Johnson\" and clicks \"Save\". After the success message, user changes the name again to \"Alice Williams\" and clicks \"Save\".\n  1138→- **Expected:** Both saves succeed with separate `PUT /api/users/:id` requests. After the second save, the name field displays \"Alice Williams\". Both updates are persisted.\n  1139→\n  1140→#### Test: Email field is displayed but not editable\n  1141→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with email \"alice@example.com\".\n  1142→- **Action:** User views the profile form.\n  1143→- **Expected:** The email \"alice@example.com\" is displayed but the field is read-only / disabled and cannot be edited.\n  1144→\n  1145→#### Test: Profile update persists across navigation\n  1146→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with bio \"Old bio\".\n  1147→- **Action:** User changes bio to \"New bio\", clicks \"Save\", then navigates to `/` (home page), then navigates back to `/profile`.\n  1148→- **Expected:** The bio field displays \"New bio\", confirming the change was persisted to the database and Redux state.\n  1149→\n  1150→### Component: BecomeHostButton\n  1151→\n  1152→#### Test: Become a Host button is visible for non-host users\n  1153→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false`.\n  1154→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1155→- **Expected:** A \"Become a Host\" button is visible on the profile page.\n  1156→\n  1157→#### Test: Become a Host button is hidden for existing hosts\n  1158→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `true`.\n  1159→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1160→- **Expected:** The \"Become a Host\" button is NOT visible on the profile page.\n  1161→\n  1162→#### Test: Clicking Become a Host sets user as host\n  1163→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`.\n  1164→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Become a Host\" button.\n  1165→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to become a host?\"). User confirms. A `POST /api/users/:id/become-host` request is sent. Upon success, the button disappears, a success message is shown (e.g., \"You are now a host!\"), and the Redux user state updates `is_host` to `true`. The \"Hosting\" link becomes available in the navigation sidebar.\n  1166→\n  1167→#### Test: Cancel Become a Host confirmation dialog\n  1168→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`. The \"Become a Host\" button is visible.\n  1169→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Become a Host\" button, then clicks \"Cancel\" in the confirmation dialog.\n  1170→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. No API call is made. The \"Become a Host\" button remains visible. `is_host` remains `false`.\n  1171→\n  1172→#### Test: Become a Host button appearance\n  1173→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`.\n  1174→- **Action:** User views the profile page.\n  1175→- **Expected:** The \"Become a Host\" button is styled with the coral/red accent color (#FF5A5F), has clear text reading \"Become a Host\", and is visually prominent on the page.\n  1176→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AcAwQJJqU6JH3s8U7y74Zn","session_id":"f65fbc7d-7519-48b6-af78-4161af35e017","uuid":"ab2453ac-c720-4c90-bb7a-6d53baf60d82"}
