hes for \"Paris\", views results, then clears the location field, types \"Tokyo\", and searches again.\n125-- **Expected:** The first search shows only Paris properties. After the second search, the grid updates to show only Tokyo properties. The location input correctly reflects \"Tokyo\".\n--\n169-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page on a narrow viewport where all chips don't fit in one row.\n...\n</persisted-output>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f65fbc7d-7519-48b6-af78-4161af35e017","uuid":"7d332417-bff1-4ef1-90eb-602ef5f265e8","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"47-- **Action:** User types \"unknown@example.com\" and clicks \"Log In\".\n48-- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"No account found with this email\"). The user remains on the login page.\n49-\n50:#### Test: Login form email input is functional on repeated use\n51-- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n52-- **Action:** User types \"wrong@example.com\", submits and gets an error, then clears the field, types \"guest@example.com\", and clicks \"Log In\" again.\n53-- **Expected:** The second submission succeeds, the user is logged in and redirected to home.\n--\n79-- **Action:** User types \"Some Name\" in the name field and \"existing@example.com\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n80-- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"An account with this email already exists\"). The user remains on the register form.\n81-\n82:#### Test: Register form fields are functional on repeated use\n83-- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n84-- **Action:** User fills in name and an already-existing email, submits and gets an error, then changes the email to a new unique email and clicks \"Register\" again.\n85-- **Expected:** The second submission succeeds, the user is registered and redirected to home.\n--\n119-- **Action:** User clears the location field (making it empty) and clicks the search button.\n120-- **Expected:** The property grid resets to show all properties (unfiltered by location).\n121-\n122:#### Test: Search bar is functional on repeated use\n123-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n124-- **Action:** User searches for \"Paris\", views results, then clears the location field, types \"Tokyo\", and searches again.\n125-- **Expected:** The first search shows only Paris properties. After the second search, the grid updates to show only Tokyo properties. The location input correctly reflects \"Tokyo\".\n--\n169-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page on a narrow viewport where all chips don't fit in one row.\n170-- **Expected:** The category filter bar is horizontally scrollable. The user can scroll left/right to see all property type chips.\n171-\n172:#### Test: Category chip is functional on repeated use\n173-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n174-- **Action:** User clicks \"Apartment\" (filtered), then clicks \"House\" (switches filter), then clicks \"House\" again (deselects), then clicks \"Cabin\" (filtered again).\n175-- **Expected:** Each click correctly updates the selected chip and the property grid filters. The final state shows only cabin properties with the \"Cabin\" chip highlighted.\n--\n241-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has previously favorited two properties. User navigates to the home page.\n242-- **Expected:** The app calls `GET /api/favorites` to fetch the user's favorites. The two favorited properties show filled/red hearts. All other properties show outline hearts.\n243-\n244:#### Test: Favorite button is functional on repeated use\n245-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page with a property that is not favorited.\n246-- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon (favorites it), then clicks it again (unfavorites it), then clicks it a third time (favorites it again).\n247-- **Expected:** Each click correctly toggles the heart appearance and makes the appropriate API call. The final state is favorited (filled heart).\n--\n306-- **Action:** User resets or clears all filter values back to their defaults (e.g., via a \"Clear Filters\" or \"Reset\" button, or manually resetting each).\n307-- **Expected:** The property grid returns to showing all properties (unfiltered). All filter controls return to their default states.\n308-\n309:#### Test: Filters panel controls are functional on repeated use\n310-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n311-- **Action:** User sets bedrooms to 3 (filtered), then changes bedrooms back to 1, then sets bathrooms to 2, then unchecks and re-checks a \"WiFi\" amenity.\n312-- **Expected:** Each change updates the property grid correctly. The final state reflects the last set of filter values (bedrooms >= 1, bathrooms >= 2, WiFi checked).\n--\n349-- **Action:** User applies a category filter by clicking the \"Cabin\" chip.\n350-- **Expected:** The pagination resets to page 1. The property grid shows the first page of filtered results. The page indicator highlights \"1\".\n351-\n352:#### Test: Pagination is functional on repeated use\n353-- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of results with multiple pages available.\n354-- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\" (goes to page 2), then clicks \"Next\" again (page 3), then clicks \"Previous\" (back to page 2), then clicks page \"1\" (back to page 1).\n355-- **Expected:** Each navigation correctly updates the property grid and page indicator. The final state shows page 1 results.\n356-\n357-## Page: Property Detail (`/properties/:id`)\n358-\n359:<!-- Components: ImageGallery, PropertyHeader, PropertyInfo, PropertyDescription, AmenitiesList, BookingCard, ReviewsSection, HostInfoCard -->\n360-\n361-### Component: ImageGallery\n362-\n--\n377-- **Action:** User clicks on the third thumbnail image.\n378-- **Expected:** The third image becomes the main large image. The previously main image moves to the thumbnail grid.\n379-\n380:#### Test: Clicking thumbnails is functional on repeated use\n381-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with multiple images.\n382-- **Action:** User clicks the second thumbnail, then the fourth thumbnail, then the first thumbnail.\n383-- **Expected:** Each click updates the main image to the clicked thumbnail. The final state shows the first thumbnail as the main image.\n--\n399-#### Test: Clicking review count scrolls to or navigates to reviews section\n400-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with reviews.\n401-- **Action:** User clicks the \"(23 reviews)\" link in the property header.\n402:- **Expected:** The page scrolls down to the ReviewsSection on the same page.\n403-\n404-#### Test: Property header displays host avatar as clickable element\n405-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page. The host has an avatar_url set.\n--\n439-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Show less\" link.\n440-- **Expected:** The description collapses back to the truncated view with \"Show more\" visible again.\n441-\n442:#### Test: Show more/less toggle is functional on repeated use\n443-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with a long description.\n444-- **Action:** User clicks \"Show more\", then \"Show less\", then \"Show more\" again.\n445-- **Expected:** Each click correctly toggles between the truncated and expanded states. The final state shows the full description.\n--\n539-- **Action:** User scrolls down the page past the booking card's initial position.\n540-- **Expected:** The booking card remains visible in a sticky sidebar position as the user scrolls through the property description, amenities, and reviews.\n541-\n542:#### Test: Booking card date pickers and guest selector are functional on repeated use\n543-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page.\n544-- **Action:** User selects check-in \"2026-05-01\" and check-out \"2026-05-04\", then changes check-in to \"2026-06-01\" and check-out to \"2026-06-05\", then changes guest count from 2 to 4 and back to 2.\n545-- **Expected:** Each change correctly updates the price breakdown. The final state shows \"2026-06-01\" to \"2026-06-05\" with 2 guests.\n546-\n547:### Component: ReviewsSection\n548-\n549:#### Test: Reviews section displays average ratings by category\n550-- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with multiple reviews. The average ratings are: cleanliness 4.5, accuracy 4.2, communication 4.8, location 4.6, value 4.0.\n551-- **Expected:** The reviews section shows a summary with average ratings for each category: \"Cleanliness: 4.5\", \"Accuracy: 4.2\", \"Communication: 4.8\", \"Location: 4.6\", \"Value: 4.0\". Each rating is displayed with a star icon or progress bar. An overall average rating is also displayed.\n552-\n553:#### Test: Reviews section displays overall average rating and total review count\n554-- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with 15 reviews and an overall average rating of 4.3.\n555-- **Expected:** The reviews section header shows a star icon with \"4.3\" and \"15 reviews\" (or similar format like \"4.3 · 15 reviews\").\n556-\n557:#### Test: Reviews section displays individual review cards\n558-- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with reviews. A review exists from guest \"Alice\" dated \"2026-01-15\" with rating 5 and comment \"Amazing place, loved every minute!\".\n559-- **Expected:** An individual review card is displayed showing the guest name \"Alice\", the date \"January 2026\" (or similar formatted date), a star rating of 5, and the comment text \"Amazing place, loved every minute!\".\n560-\n561:#### Test: Review cards display guest avatar or initial\n562-- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with reviews. A reviewer has an avatar_url set, another reviewer does not.\n563:- **Expected:** Review cards show the guest's avatar image when available. When no avatar is set, a placeholder (e.g., first initial in a circle) is displayed.\n564-\n565:#### Test: Reviews section shows message when property has no reviews\n566-- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with no reviews.\n567-- **Expected:** The reviews section displays a message like \"No reviews yet\" instead of an empty review list. Category average ratings are not shown.\n568-\n569:#### Test: Reviews section handles pagination or \"Show more\" for many reviews\n570-- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with more than 6 reviews.\n571-- **Expected:** An initial subset of reviews is displayed (e.g., 6 reviews). A \"Show all X reviews\" button is visible at the bottom (where X is the total count).\n572-\n--\n575-- **Action:** User clicks \"Show all X reviews\".\n576-- **Expected:** All review cards are displayed. The button disappears or changes to \"Show less\".\n577-\n578:#### Test: Reviews are ordered by most recent first\n579-- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with multiple reviews created on different dates.\n580:- **Expected:** Review cards are displayed in reverse chronological order, with the most recently created review appearing first.\n581-\n582-### Component: HostInfoCard\n583-\n--\n647-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n648-- **Expected:** The tab content area displays a message like \"No cancelled trips.\"\n649-\n650:#### Test: Tabs are functional on repeated use\n651-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page.\n652-- **Action:** User clicks \"Past\", then \"Cancelled\", then \"Upcoming\", then \"Past\" again.\n653-- **Expected:** Each click correctly updates the selected tab highlight and displays the correct set of bookings. The final state shows the \"Past\" tab selected with completed bookings displayed.\n--\n671-- **Action:** User clicks on the trip card (not the cancel or review button).\n672-- **Expected:** The app navigates to a booking detail view showing full booking information including property details, dates, guest count, price breakdown, and special requests.\n673-\n674:#### Test: Cancel button appears on pending bookings\n675-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"pending\" is displayed.\n676-- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Cancel\" button (or cancel icon button) that is clickable.\n677-\n678:#### Test: Cancel button appears on confirmed bookings\n679-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed.\n680-- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Cancel\" button that is clickable.\n681-\n682:#### Test: Cancel button does not appear on completed bookings\n683-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A booking with status \"completed\" is displayed.\n684-- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Cancel\" button.\n685-\n686:#### Test: Cancel button does not appear on already cancelled bookings\n687-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Cancelled\" tab. A booking with status \"cancelled\" is displayed.\n688-- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Cancel\" button.\n689-\n690:#### Test: Write Review button appears on completed bookings without a review\n691-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A booking with status \"completed\" exists that does not have an associated review.\n692:- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Write Review\" button that is clickable.\n693-\n694:#### Test: Write Review button does not appear on completed bookings that already have a review\n695-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A completed booking exists that already has an associated review.\n696:- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Write Review\" button. Instead, it may show \"Reviewed\" text or a checkmark indicating a review was already submitted.\n697-\n698:#### Test: Clicking Write Review button navigates to review page\n699-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A completed booking with id \"booking-456\" has no review.\n700:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Write Review\" button on that trip card.\n701:- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/trips/booking-456/review` (the Write Review page).\n702-\n703:#### Test: Write Review button does not appear on pending, confirmed, or cancelled bookings\n704-- **Initial state:** User is logged in. Bookings exist with statuses \"pending\", \"confirmed\", and \"cancelled\".\n705:- **Expected:** None of these trip cards display a \"Write Review\" button. The button only appears for \"completed\" bookings.\n706-\n707-#### Test: Trip cards are ordered by check-in date\n708-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. Multiple upcoming bookings exist with different check-in dates.\n--\n710-\n711-### Component: CancelBookingDialog\n712-\n713:#### Test: Clicking Cancel button opens confirmation dialog\n714-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed with a \"Cancel\" button.\n715-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the trip card.\n716-- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog/modal appears asking the user to confirm the cancellation. The dialog displays text like \"Are you sure you want to cancel this booking?\" with the property name and dates for context. Two buttons are visible: \"Confirm Cancel\" (or \"Yes, Cancel\") and \"Keep Booking\" (or \"No, Go Back\").\n717-\n718:#### Test: Confirming cancellation updates booking status to cancelled\n719-- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a confirmed booking.\n720-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirm Cancel\" (or \"Yes, Cancel\") button.\n721-- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The dialog closes. The trip card is removed from the \"Upcoming\" tab (or its status badge updates to \"Cancelled\" in red). A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking cancelled successfully\"). The booking now appears in the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n722-\n723:#### Test: Dismissing cancellation dialog keeps booking unchanged\n724-- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a pending booking.\n725-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Keep Booking\" (or \"No, Go Back\") button.\n726-- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The booking remains in its original status (pending). No API call is made. The trip card is unchanged.\n--\n739-- **Action:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on the \"Beach House\" trip card, then confirms the cancellation in the dialog.\n740-- **Expected:** The \"Beach House\" trip card is removed from the \"Upcoming\" tab. User switches to the \"Cancelled\" tab and sees the \"Beach House\" booking with a red \"Cancelled\" status badge.\n741-\n742:#### Test: Cancel dialog is functional on repeated use\n743-- **Initial state:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab with two cancellable bookings.\n744-- **Action:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on the first booking, dismisses the dialog (clicks \"Keep Booking\"), then clicks \"Cancel\" on the second booking and confirms the cancellation.\n745-- **Expected:** The first booking remains unchanged in the \"Upcoming\" tab. The second booking is cancelled and moves to the \"Cancelled\" tab. Each dialog open/close cycle works correctly.\n--\n839-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n840-- **Expected:** An \"Add Listing\" button is prominently displayed on the Listings tab (e.g., in the header area or as a floating action button). The button has clear text \"Add Listing\" or a \"+\" icon with label.\n841-\n842:#### Test: Deactivate and activate actions work on repeated use\n843-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with two active properties.\n844-- **Action:** User deactivates the first property (confirms dialog), then activates it again, then deactivates the second property.\n845-- **Expected:** Each action updates the correct property's status. The stats overview correctly reflects the current count of active listings after each action.\n--\n884-- **Action:** User clicks the \"All\" filter.\n885-- **Expected:** All bookings across all statuses are displayed again.\n886-\n887:#### Test: Status filters work on repeated use\n888-- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n889-- **Action:** User clicks \"Pending\", then \"Confirmed\", then \"All\", then \"Completed\".\n890-- **Expected:** Each filter correctly shows the appropriate subset of bookings. The active filter indicator updates correctly each time.\n--\n899-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the pending booking row.\n900-- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking the host to confirm cancellation. The dialog shows the guest name, property, and dates for context.\n901-\n902:#### Test: Confirming cancellation of a booking updates status\n903-- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a pending booking.\n904-- **Action:** User clicks the confirm button in the dialog.\n905-- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The dialog closes. The booking's status badge changes to red \"Cancelled\". The \"Cancel\" and \"Confirm\" action buttons are removed for that booking. A success message is displayed. The \"Active Bookings\" stat decreases by 1.\n--\n927-- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with bookings in all four statuses.\n928-- **Expected:** Status badges use the correct colors: \"Pending\" has a yellow badge, \"Confirmed\" has a green badge, \"Cancelled\" has a red badge, \"Completed\" has a blue badge.\n929-\n930:#### Test: Confirm and cancel actions work on repeated use\n931-- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with three pending bookings.\n932-- **Action:** User confirms the first booking, cancels the second booking (confirming the dialog), and then confirms the third booking.\n933-- **Expected:** Each action updates the correct booking. The first and third show \"Confirmed\" badges, the second shows \"Cancelled\". Stats update correctly after each action.\n--\n1024-- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n1025-- **Expected:** A validation error appears (e.g., \"At least one photo is required\"). The form does not advance.\n1026-\n1027:#### Test: Step 6 — Pricing fields displayed\n1028-- **Initial state:** User completed Step 5 and clicked \"Next\".\n1029:- **Expected:** Step 6 is displayed with numeric input fields for: price per night and cleaning fee. The price per night field is required. The cleaning fee defaults to 0. Currency formatting or prefix ($) is shown. The step indicator shows Step 6 of 7.\n1030-\n1031:#### Test: Step 6 — Entering pricing information\n1032:- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 6.\n1033-- **Action:** User enters 150 for price per night and 50 for cleaning fee.\n1034-- **Expected:** The fields display $150 and $50 respectively.\n1035-\n1036:#### Test: Step 6 — Validation requires price per night\n1037:- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 6 with price per night empty or 0.\n1038-- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n1039-- **Expected:** A validation error appears (e.g., \"Price per night is required and must be greater than 0\"). The form does not advance.\n1040-\n1041:#### Test: Step 7 — Review and publish page displayed\n1042:- **Initial state:** User completed Step 6 and clicked \"Next\".\n1043:- **Expected:** Step 7 displays a summary of all entered information: property type, title, full address (address, city, state, country), details (guests, bedrooms, beds, bathrooms), selected amenities, photo thumbnails, price per night, and cleaning fee. A \"Publish\" button and \"Back\" button are visible. The step indicator shows Step 7 of 7.\n1044-\n1045:#### Test: Step 7 — Review page shows all entered data correctly\n1046-- **Initial state:** User has filled out all steps: type \"Cabin\", title \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\", address \"123 Pine Rd, Aspen, CO, USA\", 4 guests, 2 bedrooms, 2 beds, 1 bathroom, amenities \"WiFi\" and \"Kitchen\", 2 photos, price $200/night, cleaning fee $75.\n1047-- **Expected:** The review page displays all of these values accurately. No data is missing or incorrect.\n1048-\n1049:#### Test: Publishing a new listing creates the property\n1050:- **Initial state:** User is on Step 7 (Review) with all data entered correctly.\n1051:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Publish\" button.\n1052-- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/properties` with the property data, then `POST /api/property-images` for each photo. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Listing published successfully!\"). The form closes. The new property appears in the Listings tab grid. The \"Total Listings\" stat increments by 1.\n1053-\n1054:#### Test: Back button navigates to the previous step\n1055-- **Initial state:** User is on Step 3 of the Add Listing form.\n1056-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Back\" button.\n1057-- **Expected:** The form navigates to Step 2. All previously entered data in Step 2 is preserved (city, address, etc. are still filled).\n1058-\n1059:#### Test: Cancel button closes the form without saving\n1060-- **Initial state:** User is on Step 4 of the Add Listing form with data entered in Steps 1–3.\n1061-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button.\n1062-- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking \"Discard your listing? All entered information will be lost.\" with \"Discard\" and \"Keep Editing\" buttons.\n1063-\n1064:#### Test: Confirming cancel discards the listing form\n1065-- **Initial state:** The discard confirmation dialog is open.\n1066-- **Action:** User clicks \"Discard\".\n1067-- **Expected:** The form closes. No API calls are made. The user returns to the Listings tab. No new property is created.\n1068-\n1069:#### Test: Dismissing cancel keeps the form open\n1070-- **Initial state:** The discard confirmation dialog is open.\n1071-- **Action:** User clicks \"Keep Editing\".\n1072-- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The form remains on the current step with all data preserved.\n1073-\n1074:#### Test: Step indicator shows correct progress throughout the form\n1075-- **Initial state:** User opens the Add Listing form.\n1076:- **Action:** User navigates through all 7 steps using Next/Back buttons.\n1077-- **Expected:** The step indicator accurately shows the current step (e.g., \"Step 1 of 7\", \"Step 2 of 7\", etc.) at each stage. Completed steps may show a checkmark or different styling.\n1078-\n1079:#### Test: Data persistence across steps when navigating back and forth\n1080-- **Initial state:** User has filled out Steps 1–5 and is on Step 5.\n1081-- **Action:** User clicks \"Back\" twice to Step 3, then \"Next\" twice to Step 5.\n1082-- **Expected:** All data entered in Steps 3, 4, and 5 is preserved after navigating back and forth. No data is lost.\n1083-\n1084:#### Test: Add Listing form works correctly on repeated use\n1085-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. User has already published one listing successfully.\n1086-- **Action:** User clicks \"Add Listing\" again, fills out all steps, and publishes.\n1087-- **Expected:** A second property is created successfully. Both properties appear in the Listings tab. The \"Total Listings\" stat shows the correct total.\n1088-\n1089-## Page: User Profile (`/profile`)\n1090-\n1091:<!-- Components: ProfileForm, BecomeHostButton, UserReviewsList -->\n1092-\n1093-### Component: ProfileForm\n1094-\n--\n1174-- **Action:** User views the profile page.\n1175-- **Expected:** The \"Become a Host\" button is styled with the coral/red accent color (#FF5A5F), has clear text reading \"Become a Host\", and is visually prominent on the page.\n1176-\n1177:### Component: UserReviewsList\n1178-\n1179:#### Test: Reviews list displays user's written reviews\n1180-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written 3 reviews for different properties (e.g., \"Cozy Cabin\" rated 5, \"City Apartment\" rated 3, \"Beach Villa\" rated 4).\n1181-- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1182:- **Expected:** A \"My Reviews\" section is visible showing all 3 reviews. Each review card displays: the property title, the overall rating (with filled/unfilled stars), the comment text, and the date the review was written.\n1183-\n1184:#### Test: Reviews list shows empty state for user with no reviews\n1185-- **Initial state:** User is logged in but has not written any reviews.\n1186-- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1187:- **Expected:** The \"My Reviews\" section displays an empty state message (e.g., \"You haven't written any reviews yet\") instead of review cards.\n1188-\n1189:#### Test: Review card shows rating with star display\n1190-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review with overall rating 4 out of 5.\n1191-- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1192-- **Expected:** The review card displays 4 filled stars and 1 unfilled star, matching the rating value.\n1193-\n1194:#### Test: Review card links to the reviewed property\n1195-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review for property \"Cozy Cabin\" (property ID \"abc-123\").\n1196-- **Action:** User clicks on the property title \"Cozy Cabin\" in a review card.\n1197-- **Expected:** The user is navigated to `/properties/abc-123` (the property detail page for \"Cozy Cabin\").\n1198-\n1199:#### Test: Reviews list shows review details correctly\n1200-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review with rating 5, comment \"Amazing stay! The host was very welcoming.\", for property \"Beach Villa\", dated \"2026-01-15\".\n1201-- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1202-- **Expected:** The review card displays: property title \"Beach Villa\", 5 filled stars, comment text \"Amazing stay! The host was very welcoming.\", and date \"Jan 15, 2026\".\n1203-\n1204:#### Test: Reviews list updates after writing a new review\n1205-- **Initial state:** User is logged in, on `/profile`, and has 2 existing reviews displayed.\n1206-- **Action:** User navigates to a completed booking, writes a new review, submits it, then navigates back to `/profile`.\n1207:- **Expected:** The \"My Reviews\" section now displays 3 reviews, including the newly written review with the correct property title, rating, and comment.\n1208-\n1209:#### Test: Reviews list shows multiple reviews in chronological order\n1210-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written reviews on different dates: \"Beach Villa\" on 2026-01-15, \"City Apartment\" on 2026-02-10, \"Cozy Cabin\" on 2026-03-05.\n1211-- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1212-- **Expected:** The reviews are displayed in reverse chronological order (newest first): \"Cozy Cabin\" (Mar 5, 2026), \"City Apartment\" (Feb 10, 2026), \"Beach Villa\" (Jan 15, 2026).\n1213-\n1214:## Page: Write Review (`/trips/:bookingId/review`)\n1215-\n1216:<!-- Components: ReviewForm, RatingSliders, PropertyBookingContext -->\n1217-\n1218-### Component: PropertyBookingContext\n1219-\n--\n1235-#### Test: Redirect to login if not authenticated\n1236-- **Initial state:** No user is logged in.\n1237-- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n1238:- **Expected:** The app redirects the user to `/login`. The Write Review page is not displayed.\n1239-\n1240-#### Test: Error state when booking does not exist\n1241-- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in.\n--\n1264-- **Expected:** Six rating sliders are visible with labels: \"Overall\", \"Cleanliness\", \"Accuracy\", \"Communication\", \"Location\", and \"Value\". Each slider defaults to a mid-range value (e.g., 3 out of 5) or is unset, and shows the current numeric value.\n1265-\n1266-#### Test: Adjust overall rating slider\n1267:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1268-- **Action:** User drags the \"Overall\" slider to 5.\n1269-- **Expected:** The \"Overall\" slider displays value 5. The numeric display next to the slider updates to \"5\". Other sliders remain at their previous values.\n1270-\n1271-#### Test: Adjust cleanliness rating slider\n1272:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1273-- **Action:** User drags the \"Cleanliness\" slider to 4.\n1274-- **Expected:** The \"Cleanliness\" slider displays value 4. The numeric display updates to \"4\".\n1275-\n1276-#### Test: Adjust accuracy rating slider\n1277:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1278-- **Action:** User drags the \"Accuracy\" slider to 2.\n1279-- **Expected:** The \"Accuracy\" slider displays value 2. The numeric display updates to \"2\".\n1280-\n1281-#### Test: Adjust communication rating slider\n1282:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1283-- **Action:** User drags the \"Communication\" slider to 5.\n1284-- **Expected:** The \"Communication\" slider displays value 5. The numeric display updates to \"5\".\n1285-\n1286-#### Test: Adjust location rating slider\n1287:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1288-- **Action:** User drags the \"Location\" slider to 3.\n1289-- **Expected:** The \"Location\" slider displays value 3. The numeric display updates to \"3\".\n1290-\n1291-#### Test: Adjust value rating slider\n1292:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1293-- **Action:** User drags the \"Value\" slider to 1.\n1294-- **Expected:** The \"Value\" slider displays value 1. The numeric display updates to \"1\".\n1295-\n1296-#### Test: Rating sliders enforce 1-5 range\n1297:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page.\n1298-- **Action:** User interacts with any rating slider.\n1299-- **Expected:** The slider only allows integer values from 1 to 5 inclusive. The slider cannot go below 1 or above 5.\n1300-\n1301-#### Test: Multiple sliders can be set independently\n1302:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1303-- **Action:** User sets \"Overall\" to 5, \"Cleanliness\" to 4, \"Accuracy\" to 3, \"Communication\" to 5, \"Location\" to 4, \"Value\" to 2.\n1304-- **Expected:** Each slider displays its independently set value. No slider affects another slider's value.\n1305-\n1306-#### Test: Rating slider visual feedback shows filled stars or highlighted segments\n1307:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page.\n1308-- **Action:** User sets the \"Overall\" slider to 4.\n1309-- **Expected:** The slider visually indicates the selected rating (e.g., filled stars up to 4 out of 5, or a highlighted slider track up to the 4 position). The visual feedback clearly distinguishes selected vs unselected portions.\n1310-\n1311:### Component: ReviewForm\n1312-\n1313:#### Test: Review form displays comment text area\n1314-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review` for a completed booking.\n1315-- **Expected:** A text area is visible with a placeholder such as \"Write your review...\" or \"Tell others about your experience\" for entering the review comment.\n1316-\n1317-#### Test: Submit button is visible\n1318:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page.\n1319:- **Expected:** A \"Submit Review\" button is visible at the bottom of the form.\n1320-\n1321-#### Test: Type a comment in the text area\n1322:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with an empty comment text area.\n1323-- **Action:** User types \"Amazing stay! The villa was beautiful and the host was very responsive.\" in the comment text area.\n1324-- **Expected:** The text area displays the typed text \"Amazing stay! The villa was beautiful and the host was very responsive.\"\n1325-\n1326-#### Test: Submit review with all ratings and comment\n1327:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page. User has set Overall to 5, Cleanliness to 5, Accuracy to 4, Communication to 5, Location to 4, Value to 4, and typed \"Wonderful experience, would definitely come back!\" in the comment area.\n1328:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Submit Review\" button.\n1329:- **Expected:** The review is submitted successfully via `POST /api/reviews`. The app navigates back to `/trips` (My Trips page). A success notification or message such as \"Review submitted successfully\" appears.\n1330-\n1331-#### Test: Submitted review appears on property detail page\n1332-- **Initial state:** User just submitted a review for booking-789 (property \"Oceanfront Villa\") with Overall rating 5 and comment \"Wonderful experience, would definitely come back!\".\n--\n1339-- **Expected:** The user's reviews list includes the newly submitted review for \"Oceanfront Villa\" with the correct rating and comment.\n1340-\n1341-#### Test: Submit review with ratings but no comment\n1342:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page. User has set all six rating sliders (Overall: 3, Cleanliness: 3, Accuracy: 3, Communication: 3, Location: 3, Value: 3) but left the comment text area empty.\n1343:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Submit Review\" button.\n1344-- **Expected:** The review is submitted successfully (comment is optional per the data model). The app navigates back to `/trips`.\n1345-\n1346-#### Test: Submit button is disabled when ratings are not set\n1347:- **Initial state:** User navigates to the Write Review page. No rating sliders have been adjusted from their unset/default state.\n1348:- **Expected:** The \"Submit Review\" button is disabled or grayed out, preventing submission without ratings.\n1349-\n1350-#### Test: Form validation prevents submission without all ratings\n1351:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page. User has set Overall to 5 but left other rating sliders unset.\n1352:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Submit Review\" button.\n1353-- **Expected:** The form shows a validation error indicating all ratings are required (e.g., \"Please rate all categories\"). The review is not submitted.\n1354-\n1355:#### Test: Write Review button on My Trips disappears after submitting review\n1356:- **Initial state:** User has a completed booking for \"Oceanfront Villa\" showing a \"Write Review\" button on the My Trips page.\n1357:- **Action:** User clicks \"Write Review\", fills out all ratings (all set to 4) and a comment \"Great stay!\", and clicks \"Submit Review\". User is redirected to `/trips`.\n1358:- **Expected:** The trip card for \"Oceanfront Villa\" no longer shows the \"Write Review\" button. It may show \"Reviewed\" text or a checkmark instead.\n1359-\n1360-#### Test: Navigate back from review page without submitting\n1361:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page and has set some ratings and typed partial comment text.\n1362-- **Action:** User clicks the browser back button or a \"Cancel\" / back navigation link on the page.\n1363:- **Expected:** The user is taken back to `/trips`. No review is submitted. The \"Write Review\" button still appears on the trip card.\n1364-\n1365-#### Test: Comment text area allows multi-line input\n1366:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page.\n1367-- **Action:** User types a multi-line comment: \"First line.\\nSecond line.\\nThird line.\" using Enter/Return key to create line breaks.\n1368-- **Expected:** The text area displays the comment with line breaks preserved across all three lines.\n1369-","numLines":465}}
